{"name":"Infamous","hex":"#777985","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"infamous","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a bad reputation; disreputable; notorious; unpleasant or evil; widely known, especially for something scornful.","Causing infamy; disgraceful."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infamous"}],"entries":[{"title":"Infamous (2006 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Infamous is a 2006 American drama film written and directed by Douglas McGrath. It is based on George Plimpton's 1997 book, Truman Capote: In Which Various Friends, Enemies, Acquaintances, and Detractors Recall His Turbulent Career and covers the period from the late 1950s through the mid-1960s, during which Truman Capote researched and wrote his bestseller In Cold Blood (1965)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2e/Infamous_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infamous_(2006_film)","wikidata":"Q467078"},{"title":"Infamous (2020 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Infamous is a 2020 American crime thriller film written and directed by Joshua Caldwell. It stars Bella Thorne, Jake Manley, Amber Riley, Michael Sirow and Marisa Coughlan. It follows the story of two young lovers robbing their way across the southern United States starting in Florida, posting their exploits to social media, and gaining fame and followers as a result."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/64/Infamous_2020_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infamous_(2020_film)","wikidata":"Q95483883"},{"title":"Infamous (series)","blocks":[{"text":"Infamous is a series of action-adventure video games developed by Sucker Punch Productions and published by Sony Computer Entertainment for PlayStation 3 and PlayStation 4. The series follows the adventures of Cole MacGrath, Delsin Rowe and Abigail \"Fetch\" Walker, super-powered \"Conduits\" who must decide their own destinies of becoming either good or evil."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infamous_(series)","wikidata":"Q580863"},{"title":"Infamous (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Infamous is a 2009 action-adventure video game developed by Sucker Punch Productions and published by Sony Computer Entertainment for the PlayStation 3. The player controls the protagonist Cole MacGrath, a bike messenger caught in the center of an explosion that devastates several city blocks of the fictional Empire City. The explosion sends the city into chaos while Cole finds himself with new electricity-based super powers. Though the game's story follows Cole as he uses his new abilities to restore some semblance of order to Empire City, the player is given several opportunities to use these powers for good or evil through the game's Karma system. These choices ultimately affect character growth, the reaction of the city's populace towards Cole, and finer elements of gameplay and the story."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2b/Infamous-cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infamous_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q1346174"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Toby_Jones_-_EmpireOfLightBFI121022_%2830_of_33%29_%2852448062684%29.jpg/500px-Toby_Jones_-_EmpireOfLightBFI121022_%2830_of_33%29_%2852448062684%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Toby_Jones_-_EmpireOfLightBFI121022_%2830_of_33%29_%2852448062684%29.jpg/500px-Toby_Jones_-_EmpireOfLightBFI121022_%2830_of_33%29_%2852448062684%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Toby Jones's performance was praised and renowned film critic Rex Reed wrote, \"they gave the Oscar to the wrong Truman Capote.\"[17]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AToby_Jones_-_EmpireOfLightBFI121022_(30_of_33)_(52448062684).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3e/InFamous_Collection.jpg/250px-InFamous_Collection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3e/InFamous_Collection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3e/InFamous_Collection.jpg/250px-InFamous_Collection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Infamous Collection cover art","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInFamous_Collection.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2d/InFamousElectricity.jpg/330px-InFamousElectricity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2d/InFamousElectricity.jpg/330px-InFamousElectricity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The player can use Cole to extract electricity from nearby power sources for later use.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInFamousElectricity.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/Infamous-cutscene.jpg/330px-Infamous-cutscene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/Infamous-cutscene.jpg/330px-Infamous-cutscene.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cutscene from Infamous, showing Cole discovering his new powers with his girlfriend, Trish. The game uses comic book-style cut scenes (similar to ones used in the Sly Cooper series) to extend the superhero motif further.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInfamous-cutscene.jpg"}],"so